# Cloudflare Images + Git fallback

**SOP:** `docs/sop/cloudflare-images-git-fallback.md`  
**Global settings:** `docs/sop/cloudflare-images-global-settings.json`

## Always

- Deliver photos from Cloudflare Images: `https://imagedelivery.net/byE6BTe9lNqo21V57n4aPQ/<id>/<variant>`.
- Keep the same bytes in git under `public/images/` as backup.
- Custom IDs: `{CLOUDFLARE_IMAGES_PREFIX}-{folder}-{slug}` (this repo: `cadence-hero-homepage` ↔ `/images/hero/homepage.jpg`).
- Render with `SiteImage` or `CloudflareImage` + `cfImage()` so a Cloudflare 404 falls back to git, then the SVG placeholder.
- Open Graph and JSON-LD `image` use git-tracked `/og-image.jpg` (crawlers do not run JS fallback).
- Use `CONTACT_INFO` for NAP. Do not modify `components/idx/*`.

## Do not

- Hardcode random Cloudflare UUIDs for site photos.
- Point every heading at one master PNG.
- Skip git files because “Cloudflare will have it.”
- Use Fair Housing proxies in alt text.

## New files

1. Add the file under `public/images/<folder>/<slug>.<ext>`.
2. Register it in `lib/cloudflare-images.ts` with `img('cadence-folder-slug', '/images/folder/slug.jpg')`.
3. Upload with `npm run cloudflare:images:upload` (or the next production build if `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` is set).
